# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) before running `npm run dev`.
# See HO-CAT-002 §12.2 and HO-ACC-002 §1 Amended (2026-09-26, owner decision on cross-origin
# cookies) — the browser calls the API directly, cross-origin, with credentials. For the
# `SameSite=Lax` session cookies to actually be sent, the web app and the API must be same-SITE:
# same registrable parent domain in production (separate subdomains, e.g. www.example.com /
# api.example.com, both https), and the SAME SCHEME in development — this must be
# http://localhost:5005 (the API's `http` launch profile), not an `https://localhost:7xxx`
# profile, even though both are "localhost": a scheme mismatch alone makes a request cross-SITE
# ("schemeful same-site"), and a cross-site request never carries a `SameSite=Lax` cookie, no
# matter how permissive CORS is.
#
# This also happens to satisfy HO-CAT-002's own placeholder requirement (merge note, master
# eef1621): NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL must be a syntactically valid URL even when
# NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCKS=true and nothing is actually listening on it (mocks/browser.ts's MSW
# worker intercepts every request before it reaches the network) — the old "https://localhost:7xxx"
# placeholder was not ("7xxx" isn't a numeric port, so the browser's `fetch()` throws a TypeError
# constructing the URL before MSW ever sees the request). http://localhost:5005 is a real port
# number, so this is not a live concern for the value actually used here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5005
NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCKS=true
# Optional. Server-only API origin for the storefront's Server Components (getPublic); falls back to
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL. Needed only when the server reaches the API at a different address than
# the browser does. See README "Environment variables for the storefront".
# API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5005
# Optional. Currency of a product's first price in the staff price form (default BDT).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CURRENCY_CODE=BDT
